{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Txzv1KLqTxmeaQ2hApq7HN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier scenario, based on the experiment plan. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and predict what would happen under the worst-case assumptions.\n\nKey worst-tier assumptions:\n1. CWM handles repo-level adequately (Qwen3-4B learns to compress/summarize traces)\n2. Classification ≈ generation at both function-level AND repo-level\n3. Re-repair shows no significant improvement from per-test diagnostics\n4. Block correlation effect weaker than simulated — real errors closer to i.i.d.\n\n\n5. T=1 dominance at 68.7% severely constrains the potential gains from per-test analysis even under ideal conditions\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected metric ranges for this worst-case scenario across the different experiments. The function-level classification versus CWM F1 difference should stay narrow between -0.5 and 0.5 percentage points, with multi-seed variability around 0.5-1.5 points. At the repo level, both classification and CWM approaches cluster in the 70-78 range with minimal separation, suggesting the gap between them won't exceed 2 percentage points.\n\nI'm also tracking several downstream metrics: the CWM unparseable or truncated rate, the diagnostic re-repair resolve rate gain, and how trace-then-judge compares to direct classification. These should all stay within tight bounds. Then I need to execute the planned experiments—validating the multi-seed results for classification versus CWM, running the trace-then-judge ablation, testing trajectory-level fine-tuning, scaling to 8B parameters, measuring downstream re-repair performance, and evaluating per-test prediction quality.\n\nI'm also planning stratified oracle analysis, empirical block correlation studies, the SWE-bench per-test dataset work, repo-level training, LLM-as-judge baselines, and per-test majority voting. For the multi-seed validation specifically, I'm expecting classification F1 to hover around 87 across seeds with standard deviation between 0.5-1.5, and the gap between classification and CWM should stay narrow.\n\nFor trace-then-judge, I'm anticipating roughly equivalent or slightly worse performance than direct classification since allocating tokens to tracing might hurt overall F1 by a couple points. Trajectory-level finetuning should perform comparably to per-test aggregation since it's just binary classification of resolved versus unresolved. Model scaling to 8B shows improvements for both approaches but doesn't close the gap between them. Diagnostic re-repair likely yields minimal gains, and I'm still working through the precision-recall tradeoffs for per-test evaluation.\n\nLooking at the oracle stratification, T=1 dominance means most of the potential advantage disappears. Block correlation assumptions don't match the empirical error distribution, which behaves closer to i.i.d. The SWE-bench per-test data construction should work fine, and repo-level training shows both methods converging around 73-74 F1 with negligible differences. Zero-shot LLM baselines would be weaker but useful as reference points, and majority voting provides only modest gains that don't fundamentally change the conclusions.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the full YAML response.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10614,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10614},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5a97b80-9229-4bf1-bd6c-e99b19524a4a","uuid":"d6a625d1-08e3-4f30-b069-d9caf567c6c9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Txzv1KLqTxmeaQ2hApq7HN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Abandon method-superiority framing entirely. Pivot to analysis paper:\n  \"Are Classification and Generation Equivalent for Code Execution Simulation? An Empirical Study.\"\n  Core contribution becomes the surprising negative result itself — across function-level AND repo-level,\n  reformulation doesn't matter, which challenges the intuition that generation is harder.\n  Secondary contribution: oracle frontier characterization showing per-test granularity is theoretically\n  valuable only under specific conditions (multi-F2P, block-correlated errors, regression rate >10%)\n  that rarely co-occur in practice. Efficiency angle (1-token inference) becomes a minor practical note,\n  not a claim. Claim 2 dropped. Claim 3 reframed as \"negative characterization\" — here's why per-test\n  doesn't help in practice despite theoretical appeal. Target: EMNLP Findings or pivot to ICSE 2027\n  as empirical study.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification (mvp-b) 和 CWM baseline 各跑 seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean±std F1，\n      paired bootstrap CI 检验显著性。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.05\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.82\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.85\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.91\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.25\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.95\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.60\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 1.08\n      cls_vs_cwm_overall_f1_diff_pp: -0.12\n      paired_bootstrap_p_value: 0.74\n      significant_at_005: false\n      cls_seed_results: [87.5, 86.8, 87.3]\n      cwm_seed_results: [87.5, 86.9, 87.8]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设是 classification ≈ generation at function-level。CWM baseline 已显示\n      87.51% overall accuracy（与 cls 的 87.5% 几乎相同），seed 变异（std ~0.8-1.0）远大于\n      两种方法的均值差（~0.1pp）。这是因为 function-level 代码执行输出短（通常 <20 tokens），\n      CWM 不会触发 token-budget 耗尽或复杂字符串匹配失败，4B 模型足以记忆这些简单输出模式。\n      Paired bootstrap 无法拒绝零假设，p=0.74 表明差异完全在噪声范围内。\n      std 在 0.8-1.0 范围（位于 worst 档 [0.5, 1.5] 区间中部），反映 LoRA 微调对随机初始化的\n      中等敏感性——不至于不稳定但足以淹没 <0.5pp 的方法差异。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 1: Multi-seed function-level classification vs generation (Qwen3-4B LoRA)\"\n        columns: [Method, Seed, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, Exact Match]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 0, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 1, 86.5, 87.3, 86.8, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 42, 86.9, 87.8, 87.3, \"-\"]\n          - [\"Cls Mean±Std\", \"-\", \"87.05±0.82\", \"87.85±0.91\", \"87.2±0.36\", \"-\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, 84.0]\n          - [CWM Generation, 1, 86.5, 87.1, 86.9, 83.2]\n          - [CWM Generation, 42, 87.6, 88.0, 87.8, 84.5]\n          - [\"CWM Mean±Std\", \"-\", \"87.25±0.95\", \"87.60±1.08\", \"87.4±0.46\", \"83.9±0.65\"]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls−CWM)\", \"-\", \"-0.20\", \"+0.25\", \"-0.12\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"p-value (bootstrap)\", \"-\", \"0.68\", \"0.71\", \"0.74\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing F1 distribution across 3 seeds for cls vs CWM, overlapping boxes confirm null result\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个种子的结果完全重叠，bootstrap CI 包含零。这确认了 function-level 的 null result，\n      与 worst 档假设一致。但这本身是一个有价值的发现：直觉上 generation（预测完整执行输出）\n      应该比 classification（预测 1-bit pass/fail）更难，但实证表明在 function-level 复杂度下\n      两者等价。论文可以围绕\"为什么这个直觉是错的\"展开分析。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单一 Qwen3-4B 模型训练先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。\n      与 direct classification 对比，测试显式推理是否有帮助。\n    expected_results:\n      trace_judge_pass_f1: 86.2\n      trace_judge_fail_f1: 86.8\n      trace_judge_overall_acc: 86.5\n      trace_judge_avg_trace_len_tokens: 38\n      direct_cls_pass_f1: 87.1\n      direct_cls_fail_f1: 87.9\n      f1_diff_vs_direct_cls: -0.95\n      unparseable_predictions_pct: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 trace-then-judge vs direct cls diff 在 [-2, 2] 范围。预测轻微下降（-0.95pp）\n      是因为：(1) 4B 模型容量有限，分配 ~38 tokens 给 trace 实际上消耗了本可用于判断的注意力\n      和参数容量；(2) trace 引入了额外的错误传播路径——如果 trace 中推理错误，最终 pass/fail\n      判断会被误导；(3) 1.8% 的预测因 trace 格式不规范而无法解析（direct cls 几乎不存在此问题）；\n      (4) function-level 代码足够简单，4B 模型已经能直接\"感知\"pass/fail，显式推理是冗余的。\n      这个结果在 worst 档下支持\"任务简单性\"解释——不是跳过推理有帮助，而是推理本身不必要。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 2: Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification ablation\"\n        columns: [Method, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, Unparseable %]\n        rows:\n          - [Direct Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [Trace-then-Judge, 86.2, 86.8, 86.5, 1.8]\n          - [CWM Generation, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"Δ (TtJ−Direct)\", -0.9, -1.1, -1.0, \"+1.8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing three methods' F1, showing trace-then-judge slightly below both direct cls and CWM\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 轻微劣于 direct classification 和 CWM，但差异在 1pp 以内（可能不显著）。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，这强化了\"reformulation 不重要\"的结论——无论是 generate output、\n      generate trace + judge、还是 direct classify，4B 模型在 function-level 都达到相似的性能天花板。\n      这暗示瓶颈在模型的代码理解能力而非任务表述方式。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved。\n      相同 problem_id 的所有 (code, test) 对聚合为 (code, all_tests) → resolved/unresolved。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_overall_acc: 86.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 85.8\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 86.5\n      traj_resolved_precision: 86.0\n      traj_resolved_recall: 85.6\n      per_test_aggregated_to_traj_acc: 85.5\n      per_test_agg_resolved_f1: 85.1\n      traj_vs_per_test_agg_diff_pp: 0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 模型直接学习 resolved/unresolved 二分类，在 function-level 数据上\n      准确率略低于 per-test（86.2% vs 87.5%），因为它需要在单次前向传播中综合所有测试的\n      pass/fail 状态，而 per-test 模型可以独立判断每个测试。但差距仅 ~1.3pp，因为 function-level\n      问题大多只有 1-3 个测试，trajectory-level 聚合的信息损失很小。\n      关键对比：per-test 预测聚合到 trajectory-level（用 AND 逻辑：所有测试 pass → resolved）\n      得到 85.5%，反而略低于直接 trajectory-level 训练的 86.2%，说明 per-test 聚合引入了\n      错误累积（任何一个 per-test 假阴性都会导致 trajectory 误判）。\n      这在 worst 档下意味着 per-test 粒度不仅没有方法论优势，聚合时还有误差放大的劣势。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 3: Per-test vs Trajectory-level verification (function-level)\"\n        columns: [Method, Granularity, Resolved F1, Unresolved F1, Overall Acc]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification (per-test), \"Per-test\", \"-\", \"-\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Cls aggregated → traj\", \"Per-test→Traj\", 85.1, 85.8, 85.5]\n          - [Traj-level fine-tuned, \"Trajectory\", 85.8, 86.5, 86.2]\n          - [CWM (per-test), \"Per-test\", \"-\", \"-\", 87.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Comparison bar chart showing per-test models outperform at per-test level but lose advantage when aggregated to trajectory level\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test 粒度在聚合时的误差累积效应是 worst 档的关键 negative finding。\n      即使 per-test 准确率更高（87.5% vs 86.2%），AND 聚合逻辑使得每个 per-test\n      的假阳性/假阴性都会传播到 trajectory 判断。在 T=1 主导的 function-level 数据中\n      这个问题不显著，但它预示了 per-test 方法在实践中的局限性。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      将 classification 和 CWM 模型从 4B 扩展到 8B，观察准确率变化和方法间差距是否改变。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.8\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.3\n      cls_8b_overall_acc: 90.1\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.5\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 90.0\n      cwm_8b_overall_acc: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.2\n      cls_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp: 2.6\n      cwm_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp: 2.3\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp: 0.3\n      cls_vs_cwm_4b_gap_pp: -0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型容量翻倍，两种方法都获得 ~2.5pp 提升，但 cls vs cwm gap 仍然在噪声范围内\n      （0.3pp at 8B vs ~0pp at 4B）。这是因为 function-level 的执行输出在 8B 规模下\n      更容易精确预测（exact match 84% → 87.2%），CWM 的提升与 cls 同步。\n      Worst 档假设 CWM 在 function-level 没有本质困难，8B 只是让两种方法同等程度地接近\n      天花板。gap 没有随规模扩大而扩大（或缩小），进一步确认等价性不是 4B 的偶然现象，\n      而是 function-level 任务的内在属性。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 4: Scaling behavior — Classification vs CWM at 4B and 8B\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, \"Δ vs CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 4B, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"+0.0\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 8B, 89.8, 90.3, 90.1, \"+0.3\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 8B, 89.5, 90.0, 89.8, \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot with model size (4B, 8B) on x-axis, F1 on y-axis, showing parallel scaling curves for cls and CWM\"\n    analysis: >\n      平行缩放曲线是 worst 档最清晰的 visual evidence：两种方法受益于规模增长的程度相同，\n      差距不随规模变化。这排除了\"4B 时 CWM 受限于容量，更大模型会拉开差距\"的替代假说。\n      在 pivot 论文中，这成为 equivalence 结论的强支撑——reformulation 差异在至少 4B-8B\n      范围内是规模无关的。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上测量 per-test failure 预测的 precision/recall，评估诊断信号质量。\n    expected_results:\n      fail_prediction_precision: 83.5\n      fail_prediction_recall: 86.8\n      pass_prediction_precision: 87.4\n      pass_prediction_recall: 84.0\n      per_problem_all_tests_correct_pct: 72.3\n      per_problem_at_least_one_wrong_pct: 27.7\n      false_positive_fail_rate: 16.0\n      false_negative_fail_rate: 13.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-test fail prediction precision 83.5% 意味着每 6 个 predicted-fail 中约有 1 个\n      是误报（实际 pass 的测试被预测为 fail）。在 worst 档下这个精度不足以提供可靠的\n      诊断信号：如果你告诉修复代理\"test_X 失败了\"但实际没有，代理会浪费时间修复不存在的问题。\n      Recall 86.8% 意味着约 13% 的真实失败测试被漏掉，这些被遗漏的失败可能恰好是最难预测的\n      边界情况。72.3% 的 problem 能完美预测所有测试，但剩余 27.7% 的 problem 至少有一个\n      测试判断错误——足以导致错误的诊断建议。\n      这些数字在 function-level 上尚可，但预示 repo-level（更长的测试、更复杂的行为）会更差。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 5: Per-test failure prediction quality\"\n        columns: [Metric, Pass, Fail, Macro Avg]\n        rows:\n          - [Precision, 87.4, 83.5, 85.5]\n          - [Recall, 84.0, 86.8, 85.4]\n          - [F1, 85.7, 85.1, 85.4]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap for per-test pass/fail predictions\"\n      - \"Per-problem accuracy histogram showing long tail of partially-correct predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic signal 质量中等——足以说明模型学到了测试语义，但 precision 不足以\n      可靠指导修复。这为 Claim 2 的降级提供数据支撑：per-test 预测确实包含信息，\n      但噪声水平限制了下游实用性。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P 测试数量（T=1, T=2, T=3+）分层的 oracle 分析，\n      展示 per-test 优势集中在 multi-test instances。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage_pp: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage_pp: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 15.8\n      T2_iid_advantage_pp: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage_pp: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.5\n      T3plus_iid_advantage_pp: 0.312\n      T3plus_block_advantage_pp: 0.498\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.072\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.191\n      T1_dominance_dilution_factor: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=1 占 68.7% 的 instances（已由 oracle-total-validated 确认），在这些 instances 中\n      per-test 和 trajectory-level 在数学上等价（只有一个 F2P 测试，预测它就等于预测整体）。\n      因此 T=1 的 iid advantage 几乎为零（0.02pp），仅来自随机波动。\n      T=2 和 T=3+ 分别占 15.8% 和 15.5%，在这些子集中 per-test 确实有优势（T=2: 0.185pp iid,\n      T=3+: 0.312pp iid），但被 T=1 的 68.7% 权重严重稀释。\n      Block-correlated 设定下优势更大（T=1: 0.109pp），但 worst 档假设 real errors closer to\n      i.i.d.，所以 block 优势在实际中不可达。\n      加权平均 iid advantage 仅 0.072pp——这是 worst 档下 per-test 方法的实际预期收益，\n      几乎没有实用意义。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 6: Oracle per-test advantage stratified by F2P test count\"\n        columns: [\"T (F2P count)\", \"% Instances\", \"iid Adv (pp)\", \"Block Adv (pp)\", \"Weighted iid Contrib\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 68.7, 0.020, 0.109, 0.014]\n          - [2, 15.8, 0.185, 0.362, 0.029]\n          - [\"3+\", 15.5, 0.312, 0.498, 0.048]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", 100.0, 0.072, 0.191, \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: x-axis T buckets, y-axis per-test advantage; area proportional to instance count shows dilution effect\"\n      - \"Pie chart showing T=1 dominance in SWE-bench Verified\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档叙事的核心支撑图表。视觉上清晰展示了\"理论优势存在但被分布稀释\"的故事。\n      T=1 的巨大占比（68.7%）使得 per-test 的理论优势在实践中几乎消失。\n      论文可以用这个 finding 作为 Claim 3 的\"negative characterization\"核心：\n      per-test 不是无用的，而是有用的条件（T≥2, block-correlated errors, regression rate >10%）\n      太少同时满足。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      给修复代理提供 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test 信息，\n      在 200 个 instances 上比较 resolve rate。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 28.5\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 29.0\n      resolve_rate_gain_pp: 0.5\n      gain_significant: false\n      p_value: 0.62\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 4\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 3\n      net_helped: 1\n      diagnostic_precision_on_test_set: 78.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档 gain 在 [-0.5, 1] pp 范围。预测 +0.5pp（29.0% vs 28.5%），原因：\n      (1) 68.7% T=1 instances 中 per-test 信息与 trajectory-level 等价，提供 per-test\n      预测不增加任何信息；(2) 在 T≥2 instances（~31%，约 62/200 个）中，per-test 预测\n      的 precision ~78% 引入了约 22% 的错误诊断，修复代理可能基于错误信息做出更差的修复；\n      (3) 4 个 instances 中诊断确实帮助了定位（多测试场景中正确识别了失败的特定测试），\n      但 3 个 instances 中错误诊断反而误导了修复方向；(4) 净增益 1 个 instance（+0.5pp on 200），\n      统计上远不显著。\n      这确认了 worst 档假设：per-test diagnostics 的理论价值被预测噪声和 T=1 主导效应\n      共同消解。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 7: Diagnostic re-repair experiment\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve Rate (%), \"Δ vs Baseline\", p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No diagnostic (baseline)\", 28.5, \"-\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"With per-test diagnostic\", 29.0, \"+0.5\", 0.62]\n          - [\"Oracle per-test (upper bound)\", 33.2, \"+4.7\", 0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: three conditions (baseline, predicted diagnostic, oracle diagnostic) showing oracle ceiling vs achievable gain\"\n    analysis: >\n      Oracle per-test 上界（33.2%）表明 per-test 信息在理想条件下有价值（+4.7pp），\n      但 predicted diagnostic 只能实现其中很小一部分（+0.5pp）。\n      Gap 来自两个方面：(a) 预测误差使诊断不可靠；(b) 修复代理本身对诊断信号的利用效率有限。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，Claim 2 被降级为\"hypothesis with oracle ceiling analysis\"，\n      不作为论文的实证贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练好的模型 per-test 预测中测量实际预测误差相关结构，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-correlated 仿真模型对比。\n    expected_results:\n      measured_intra_problem_error_correlation: 0.08\n      iid_expected_correlation: 0.0\n      block_model_assumed_correlation: 0.45\n      fraction_explained_by_iid: 0.82\n      fraction_explained_by_block: 0.18\n      cramer_v_problem_vs_error: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：\"block correlation effect weaker than simulated — real errors closer to i.i.d.\"\n      实测 intra-problem error correlation 仅 0.08（接近 i.i.d. 的 0.0，远低于 block model\n      假设的 0.45）。这意味着同一问题不同测试的预测误差之间几乎独立。\n      原因：(1) 模型对每个 (code, test) 对独立做前向传播，没有跨测试的信息共享，因此误差\n      不自然聚类；(2) function-level 测试之间差异较大（不同输入-输出对），即使对同一函数，\n      不同测试的难度分布接近均匀而非聚类；(3) Cramér's V = 0.06 表明 problem_id 对误差\n      模式几乎没有解释力。\n      这直接打击了 oracle simulation 中 block-correlated 设定的外部有效性——那些设定下\n      per-test 优势高达 0.36-0.50pp，但如果实际是近 i.i.d.，优势降至 0.02-0.07pp。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 8: Prediction error correlation structure\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Intra-problem ρ\", \"Per-test Adv (oracle, pp)\", \"Fit to Data (R²)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"i.i.d. (ρ=0)\", 0.00, \"0.020–0.072\", 0.82]\n          - [\"Block (ρ=0.45)\", 0.45, \"0.109–0.498\", 0.18]\n          - [\"Measured\", 0.08, \"0.025–0.095 (interpolated)\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot of predicted errors for test pairs within same problem, showing near-zero correlation\"\n      - \"QQ plot of empirical error correlation vs i.i.d. and block model predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档中 Claim 3 \"negative characterization\" 的关键实证。\n      Oracle simulation 的 block-correlated 设定 over-estimated per-test advantage by ~5×。\n      论文应诚实报告这一点：block correlation 是理论上合理的假设，但在 4B LoRA 模型的\n      实际预测中不成立。这不否定 oracle 分析的价值——它揭示了 per-test 有用的理论条件——\n      但将 \"when does per-test help?\" 的答案从 \"often\" 修正为 \"rarely in practice\"。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Per-Test Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重新评估 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels。\n      构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_evaluations: 462\n      failed_docker_builds: 23\n      timeout_evaluations: 15\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 117408\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 15.9\n      avg_f2p_tests_per_instance: 2.3\n      avg_p2p_tests_per_instance: 13.6\n      pass_rate_overall: 0.71\n      fail_rate_overall: 0.29\n      construction_time_hours: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据集构建本身是工程任务，worst 档不影响其成功率——Docker 评估的失败率（23 build failures\n      + 15 timeouts = 7.6%）来自 SWE-bench 已知的环境不稳定性而非方法论问题。\n      关键数据特征：avg F2P tests = 2.3（与 oracle simulation 的 T_mean=2.3 一致），\n      avg P2P tests = 13.6，说明 repo-level 确实有更多测试可以利用 per-test 粒度。\n      但 worst 档下这些额外测试不会转化为 per-test 优势（见 repo-level-training 预测）。\n      Pass rate 71% 表示大多数 candidate patches 通过大多数测试——修复任务的 baseline\n      不低，这使得增量改进更难显著。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 9: SWE-bench-PerTest dataset statistics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Instances (successful), 462]\n          - [Candidates per instance, \"16 (mean)\"]\n          - [Total (code, test) pairs, \"117,408\"]\n          - [F2P tests per instance (mean), 2.3]\n          - [P2P tests per instance (mean), 13.6]\n          - [Overall pass rate, \"71%\"]\n          - [Overall fail rate, \"29%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of F2P test count distribution, confirming T=1 mode and long tail\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集本身是一个 resource contribution，即使在 worst 档下也有独立价值。\n      分布特征确认了 oracle simulation 的假设（T distribution, pass/fail ratio），\n      为后续 repo-level experiments 提供了可靠的数据基础。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training (Classification vs CWM)\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上微调 Qwen3-4B/8B classification 和 CWM 模型，\n      评估 repo-level 性能和 cls vs cwm gap。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_repo_f1: 73.8\n      cwm_4b_repo_f1: 73.2\n      cls_vs_cwm_4b_gap_pp: 0.6\n      cls_8b_repo_f1: 76.5\n      cwm_8b_repo_f1: 76.1\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp: 0.4\n      cwm_4b_unparseable_pct: 3.8\n      cwm_4b_truncated_pct: 1.2\n      cwm_8b_unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      cwm_8b_truncated_pct: 0.8\n      cwm_4b_exact_match: 52.3\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 58.7\n      func_to_repo_cls_drop_pp: 13.7\n      func_to_repo_cwm_drop_pp: 14.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：\"CWM handles repo-level adequately (Qwen3-4B learns to compress/summarize traces)\"\n      和 \"Classification ≈ generation at repo-level\"。\n      \n      Repo-level gap 仅 0.6pp (4B) / 0.4pp (8B)，在 worst 档范围 [-1, 2] 内偏低端。原因：\n      (1) Qwen3-4B 学会了对 repo-level 长输出进行摘要式预测——不精确复现完整 trace，但\n      输出足够接近以判断 pass/fail。CWM 的 exact match 低（52.3%），但因为模型学到了\n      \"输出的关键语义模式\"（如 assertion error keywords、expected vs actual 值的判断），\n      即使字面不匹配，分类判断仍然正确；\n      (2) unparseable + truncated 仅 5%（3.8% + 1.2%），在 worst 档范围 [0, 5] 上限，\n      说明模型确实学会了在 token budget 内生成可解析的输出；\n      (3) 两种方法从 func-level 到 repo-level 都下降了 ~14pp（cls: 87.5→73.8, cwm: 87.5→73.2），\n      下降程度几乎相同，说明复杂度增加对两种方法的影响是均匀的；\n      (4) 8B 模型下 gap 更小（0.4pp），进一步确认等价性随规模增大而加强。\n      \n      这是 worst 档的定义性结果：repo-level 也没有打破等价性。论文必须完全放弃\n      \"complexity-dependent advantage\" 的 framing。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 10: Repo-level Classification vs CWM (SWE-bench-PerTest)\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, F1, \"Exact Match\", \"Unparseable %\", \"Truncated %\", \"Δ Cls−CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 4B, 73.8, \"-\", 0.0, 0.0, \"+0.6\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, 73.2, 52.3, 3.8, 1.2, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 8B, 76.5, \"-\", 0.0, 0.0, \"+0.4\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 8B, 76.1, 58.7, 2.1, 0.8, \"-\"]\n      - caption: \"Table 11: Function-level to Repo-level performance drop\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Func F1\", \"Repo F1\", \"Drop (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 87.5, 73.8, -13.7]\n          - [CWM Generation, 87.5, 73.2, -14.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: func-level vs repo-level F1 for cls and CWM, showing parallel drop\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: CWM exact match vs binary accuracy on repo-level, showing low exact match can coexist with decent binary accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      CWM 的 exact match 从 func-level 84% 暴跌至 repo-level 52%，但 F1 仅从 87.5 降至 73.2。\n      这个 disconnect 是 worst 档的核心反直觉发现：CWM 的\"失败模式\"（truncation、近似输出）\n      并没有导致分类性能的对应崩溃，因为模型学会了从不完美的生成中仍然提取 pass/fail 信号。\n      这挑战了原始论文 framing 中\"CWM failure modes dominate at repo-level\"的假设。\n      \n      论文 pivot：这个发现本身是有趣的分析贡献——\"为什么 generation 在字面意义上失败\n      但在语义意义上成功\"可以成为分析论文的一个 section。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge baseline（trajectory-level 和 per-test），\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的参考点。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_f1: 68.5\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_f1: 66.2\n      qwen3_32b_traj_f1: 74.8\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_f1: 73.1\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_unparseable_pct: 8.3\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_unparseable_pct: 4.1\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_8b_gap: 19.0\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_32b_gap: 12.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 在 function-level 上表现显著低于微调 4B 模型，因为：\n      (1) 没有针对特定 pass/fail 判断格式的训练，输出不稳定且 unparseable 率较高；\n      (2) 32B 的上下文理解能力更强，缩小了差距但仍低于微调 4B（74.8 vs 87.5），\n      说明 task-specific fine-tuning 的价值大于 model scale 的差异；\n      (3) per-test 始终略低于 trajectory（~2pp），因为 zero-shot 模型需要更明确的\n      判断格式指导，per-test 的结构化输出对 zero-shot 更难。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，这些 baseline 提供 Pareto frontier 参考：\n      fine-tuned 4B > zero-shot 32B >> zero-shot 8B，确认 fine-tuning 是必要的。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 12: LLM-as-Judge baselines vs fine-tuned models\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, Fine-tuned, \"Traj F1\", \"Per-test F1\", \"Unparseable %\"]\n        rows:\n          - [LLM-Judge, 8B, No, 68.5, 66.2, 8.3]\n          - [LLM-Judge, 32B, No, 74.8, 73.1, 4.1]\n          - [Classification, 4B, Yes, \"-\", 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, Yes, \"-\", 87.5, 0.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: x-axis = model size (or FLOPs), y-axis = F1, showing fine-tuned 4B dominating zero-shot 32B\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B 显著优于 zero-shot 32B 这一结果在任何 tier 下都成立，\n      不受 worst 档的 cls-vs-cwm 等价性影响。这为 pivot 论文提供了一个次要但\n      坚实的贡献：即使 classification 和 generation 等价，fine-tuning 的效率优势\n      （4B fine-tuned > 32B zero-shot）是明确的实用结论。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Per-test majority voting (K=3)，测试 self-consistency 是否提升 per-test 准确率。\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 87.5\n      majority_k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      majority_k3_fail_f1: 88.9\n      majority_k3_overall_acc: 88.6\n      gain_from_voting_pp: 1.1\n      voting_vs_8b_single_pass: -1.5\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 带来温和提升（+1.1pp），因为 self-consistency 修正了部分边界\n      预测。但收益有限的原因：(1) 4B 模型的 3 次推理采样在大多数 confident predictions\n      上完全一致（~85% 的测试三次结果相同），仅 ~15% 的 uncertain cases 从投票中受益；\n      (2) 3× inference cost 换取 1.1pp gain 的 cost-effectiveness 远低于直接用 8B\n      单次推理（+2.6pp）；(3) 在 worst 档下，voting 对 cls 和 cwm 的提升幅度相似，\n      不改变两者等价的结论。\n      这是 P2 优先级实验，在 worst 档叙事中仅作为 minor practical note。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 13: Majority voting ablation\"\n        columns: [Method, K, F1, \"Δ vs K=1\", \"Cost (×)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 1, 87.5, \"-\", \"1×\"]\n          - [Classification, 3, 88.6, \"+1.1\", \"3×\"]\n          - [Classification (8B), 1, 90.1, \"+2.6\", \"~2× (params)\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 是一个合理但不显著的优化。在 worst 档 pivot 论文中，\n      可以在 appendix 中报告以展示方法的 thoroughness，但不影响核心叙事。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10614,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10614},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5a97b80-9229-4bf1-bd6c-e99b19524a4a","uuid":"829c6d3c-9e72-4b21-9ce7-43d76408750d"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":253855,"duration_api_ms":256352,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Abandon method-superiority framing entirely. Pivot to analysis paper:\n  \"Are Classification and Generation Equivalent for Code Execution Simulation? An Empirical Study.\"\n  Core contribution becomes the surprising negative result itself — across function-level AND repo-level,\n  reformulation doesn't matter, which challenges the intuition that generation is harder.\n  Secondary contribution: oracle frontier characterization showing per-test granularity is theoretically\n  valuable only under specific conditions (multi-F2P, block-correlated errors, regression rate >10%)\n  that rarely co-occur in practice. Efficiency angle (1-token inference) becomes a minor practical note,\n  not a claim. Claim 2 dropped. Claim 3 reframed as \"negative characterization\" — here's why per-test\n  doesn't help in practice despite theoretical appeal. Target: EMNLP Findings or pivot to ICSE 2027\n  as empirical study.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification (mvp-b) 和 CWM baseline 各跑 seeds {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean±std F1，\n      paired bootstrap CI 检验显著性。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_pass_f1_mean: 87.05\n      cls_pass_f1_std: 0.82\n      cls_fail_f1_mean: 87.85\n      cls_fail_f1_std: 0.91\n      cwm_pass_f1_mean: 87.25\n      cwm_pass_f1_std: 0.95\n      cwm_fail_f1_mean: 87.60\n      cwm_fail_f1_std: 1.08\n      cls_vs_cwm_overall_f1_diff_pp: -0.12\n      paired_bootstrap_p_value: 0.74\n      significant_at_005: false\n      cls_seed_results: [87.5, 86.8, 87.3]\n      cwm_seed_results: [87.5, 86.9, 87.8]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设是 classification ≈ generation at function-level。CWM baseline 已显示\n      87.51% overall accuracy（与 cls 的 87.5% 几乎相同），seed 变异（std ~0.8-1.0）远大于\n      两种方法的均值差（~0.1pp）。这是因为 function-level 代码执行输出短（通常 <20 tokens），\n      CWM 不会触发 token-budget 耗尽或复杂字符串匹配失败，4B 模型足以记忆这些简单输出模式。\n      Paired bootstrap 无法拒绝零假设，p=0.74 表明差异完全在噪声范围内。\n      std 在 0.8-1.0 范围（位于 worst 档 [0.5, 1.5] 区间中部），反映 LoRA 微调对随机初始化的\n      中等敏感性——不至于不稳定但足以淹没 <0.5pp 的方法差异。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 1: Multi-seed function-level classification vs generation (Qwen3-4B LoRA)\"\n        columns: [Method, Seed, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, Exact Match]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 0, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 1, 86.5, 87.3, 86.8, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 42, 86.9, 87.8, 87.3, \"-\"]\n          - [\"Cls Mean±Std\", \"-\", \"87.05±0.82\", \"87.85±0.91\", \"87.2±0.36\", \"-\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, 84.0]\n          - [CWM Generation, 1, 86.5, 87.1, 86.9, 83.2]\n          - [CWM Generation, 42, 87.6, 88.0, 87.8, 84.5]\n          - [\"CWM Mean±Std\", \"-\", \"87.25±0.95\", \"87.60±1.08\", \"87.4±0.46\", \"83.9±0.65\"]\n          - [\"Δ (Cls−CWM)\", \"-\", \"-0.20\", \"+0.25\", \"-0.12\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"p-value (bootstrap)\", \"-\", \"0.68\", \"0.71\", \"0.74\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot showing F1 distribution across 3 seeds for cls vs CWM, overlapping boxes confirm null result\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个种子的结果完全重叠，bootstrap CI 包含零。这确认了 function-level 的 null result，\n      与 worst 档假设一致。但这本身是一个有价值的发现：直觉上 generation（预测完整执行输出）\n      应该比 classification（预测 1-bit pass/fail）更难，但实证表明在 function-level 复杂度下\n      两者等价。论文可以围绕\"为什么这个直觉是错的\"展开分析。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单一 Qwen3-4B 模型训练先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail。\n      与 direct classification 对比，测试显式推理是否有帮助。\n    expected_results:\n      trace_judge_pass_f1: 86.2\n      trace_judge_fail_f1: 86.8\n      trace_judge_overall_acc: 86.5\n      trace_judge_avg_trace_len_tokens: 38\n      direct_cls_pass_f1: 87.1\n      direct_cls_fail_f1: 87.9\n      f1_diff_vs_direct_cls: -0.95\n      unparseable_predictions_pct: 1.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档下 trace-then-judge vs direct cls diff 在 [-2, 2] 范围。预测轻微下降（-0.95pp）\n      是因为：(1) 4B 模型容量有限，分配 ~38 tokens 给 trace 实际上消耗了本可用于判断的注意力\n      和参数容量；(2) trace 引入了额外的错误传播路径——如果 trace 中推理错误，最终 pass/fail\n      判断会被误导；(3) 1.8% 的预测因 trace 格式不规范而无法解析（direct cls 几乎不存在此问题）；\n      (4) function-level 代码足够简单，4B 模型已经能直接\"感知\"pass/fail，显式推理是冗余的。\n      这个结果在 worst 档下支持\"任务简单性\"解释——不是跳过推理有帮助，而是推理本身不必要。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 2: Trace-then-Judge vs Direct Classification ablation\"\n        columns: [Method, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, Unparseable %]\n        rows:\n          - [Direct Classification, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [Trace-then-Judge, 86.2, 86.8, 86.5, 1.8]\n          - [CWM Generation, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [\"Δ (TtJ−Direct)\", -0.9, -1.1, -1.0, \"+1.8\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart comparing three methods' F1, showing trace-then-judge slightly below both direct cls and CWM\"\n    analysis: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 轻微劣于 direct classification 和 CWM，但差异在 1pp 以内（可能不显著）。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，这强化了\"reformulation 不重要\"的结论——无论是 generate output、\n      generate trace + judge、还是 direct classify，4B 模型在 function-level 都达到相似的性能天花板。\n      这暗示瓶颈在模型的代码理解能力而非任务表述方式。\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved。\n      相同 problem_id 的所有 (code, test) 对聚合为 (code, all_tests) → resolved/unresolved。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_overall_acc: 86.2\n      traj_resolved_f1: 85.8\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 86.5\n      traj_resolved_precision: 86.0\n      traj_resolved_recall: 85.6\n      per_test_aggregated_to_traj_acc: 85.5\n      per_test_agg_resolved_f1: 85.1\n      traj_vs_per_test_agg_diff_pp: 0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 模型直接学习 resolved/unresolved 二分类，在 function-level 数据上\n      准确率略低于 per-test（86.2% vs 87.5%），因为它需要在单次前向传播中综合所有测试的\n      pass/fail 状态，而 per-test 模型可以独立判断每个测试。但差距仅 ~1.3pp，因为 function-level\n      问题大多只有 1-3 个测试，trajectory-level 聚合的信息损失很小。\n      关键对比：per-test 预测聚合到 trajectory-level（用 AND 逻辑：所有测试 pass → resolved）\n      得到 85.5%，反而略低于直接 trajectory-level 训练的 86.2%，说明 per-test 聚合引入了\n      错误累积（任何一个 per-test 假阴性都会导致 trajectory 误判）。\n      这在 worst 档下意味着 per-test 粒度不仅没有方法论优势，聚合时还有误差放大的劣势。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 3: Per-test vs Trajectory-level verification (function-level)\"\n        columns: [Method, Granularity, Resolved F1, Unresolved F1, Overall Acc]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification (per-test), \"Per-test\", \"-\", \"-\", 87.5]\n          - [\"Cls aggregated → traj\", \"Per-test→Traj\", 85.1, 85.8, 85.5]\n          - [Traj-level fine-tuned, \"Trajectory\", 85.8, 86.5, 86.2]\n          - [CWM (per-test), \"Per-test\", \"-\", \"-\", 87.5]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Comparison bar chart showing per-test models outperform at per-test level but lose advantage when aggregated to trajectory level\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-test 粒度在聚合时的误差累积效应是 worst 档的关键 negative finding。\n      即使 per-test 准确率更高（87.5% vs 86.2%），AND 聚合逻辑使得每个 per-test\n      的假阳性/假阴性都会传播到 trajectory 判断。在 T=1 主导的 function-level 数据中\n      这个问题不显著，但它预示了 per-test 方法在实践中的局限性。\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      将 classification 和 CWM 模型从 4B 扩展到 8B，观察准确率变化和方法间差距是否改变。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_8b_pass_f1: 89.8\n      cls_8b_fail_f1: 90.3\n      cls_8b_overall_acc: 90.1\n      cwm_8b_pass_f1: 89.5\n      cwm_8b_fail_f1: 90.0\n      cwm_8b_overall_acc: 89.8\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 87.2\n      cls_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp: 2.6\n      cwm_4b_vs_8b_gain_pp: 2.3\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp: 0.3\n      cls_vs_cwm_4b_gap_pp: -0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型容量翻倍，两种方法都获得 ~2.5pp 提升，但 cls vs cwm gap 仍然在噪声范围内\n      （0.3pp at 8B vs ~0pp at 4B）。这是因为 function-level 的执行输出在 8B 规模下\n      更容易精确预测（exact match 84% → 87.2%），CWM 的提升与 cls 同步。\n      Worst 档假设 CWM 在 function-level 没有本质困难，8B 只是让两种方法同等程度地接近\n      天花板。gap 没有随规模扩大而扩大（或缩小），进一步确认等价性不是 4B 的偶然现象，\n      而是 function-level 任务的内在属性。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 4: Scaling behavior — Classification vs CWM at 4B and 8B\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, Pass F1, Fail F1, Overall Acc, \"Δ vs CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 4B, 87.1, 87.9, 87.5, \"+0.0\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, 87.3, 87.7, 87.5, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 8B, 89.8, 90.3, 90.1, \"+0.3\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 8B, 89.5, 90.0, 89.8, \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot with model size (4B, 8B) on x-axis, F1 on y-axis, showing parallel scaling curves for cls and CWM\"\n    analysis: >\n      平行缩放曲线是 worst 档最清晰的 visual evidence：两种方法受益于规模增长的程度相同，\n      差距不随规模变化。这排除了\"4B 时 CWM 受限于容量，更大模型会拉开差距\"的替代假说。\n      在 pivot 论文中，这成为 equivalence 结论的强支撑——reformulation 差异在至少 4B-8B\n      范围内是规模无关的。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Precision-Recall Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上测量 per-test failure 预测的 precision/recall，评估诊断信号质量。\n    expected_results:\n      fail_prediction_precision: 83.5\n      fail_prediction_recall: 86.8\n      pass_prediction_precision: 87.4\n      pass_prediction_recall: 84.0\n      per_problem_all_tests_correct_pct: 72.3\n      per_problem_at_least_one_wrong_pct: 27.7\n      false_positive_fail_rate: 16.0\n      false_negative_fail_rate: 13.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-test fail prediction precision 83.5% 意味着每 6 个 predicted-fail 中约有 1 个\n      是误报（实际 pass 的测试被预测为 fail）。在 worst 档下这个精度不足以提供可靠的\n      诊断信号：如果你告诉修复代理\"test_X 失败了\"但实际没有，代理会浪费时间修复不存在的问题。\n      Recall 86.8% 意味着约 13% 的真实失败测试被漏掉，这些被遗漏的失败可能恰好是最难预测的\n      边界情况。72.3% 的 problem 能完美预测所有测试，但剩余 27.7% 的 problem 至少有一个\n      测试判断错误——足以导致错误的诊断建议。\n      这些数字在 function-level 上尚可，但预示 repo-level（更长的测试、更复杂的行为）会更差。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 5: Per-test failure prediction quality\"\n        columns: [Metric, Pass, Fail, Macro Avg]\n        rows:\n          - [Precision, 87.4, 83.5, 85.5]\n          - [Recall, 84.0, 86.8, 85.4]\n          - [F1, 85.7, 85.1, 85.4]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap for per-test pass/fail predictions\"\n      - \"Per-problem accuracy histogram showing long tail of partially-correct predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Diagnostic signal 质量中等——足以说明模型学到了测试语义，但 precision 不足以\n      可靠指导修复。这为 Claim 2 的降级提供数据支撑：per-test 预测确实包含信息，\n      但噪声水平限制了下游实用性。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P-Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P 测试数量（T=1, T=2, T=3+）分层的 oracle 分析，\n      展示 per-test 优势集中在 multi-test instances。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 68.7\n      T1_iid_advantage_pp: 0.020\n      T1_block_advantage_pp: 0.109\n      T2_pct_instances: 15.8\n      T2_iid_advantage_pp: 0.185\n      T2_block_advantage_pp: 0.362\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 15.5\n      T3plus_iid_advantage_pp: 0.312\n      T3plus_block_advantage_pp: 0.498\n      weighted_avg_iid_advantage: 0.072\n      weighted_avg_block_advantage: 0.191\n      T1_dominance_dilution_factor: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      T=1 占 68.7% 的 instances（已由 oracle-total-validated 确认），在这些 instances 中\n      per-test 和 trajectory-level 在数学上等价（只有一个 F2P 测试，预测它就等于预测整体）。\n      因此 T=1 的 iid advantage 几乎为零（0.02pp），仅来自随机波动。\n      T=2 和 T=3+ 分别占 15.8% 和 15.5%，在这些子集中 per-test 确实有优势（T=2: 0.185pp iid,\n      T=3+: 0.312pp iid），但被 T=1 的 68.7% 权重严重稀释。\n      Block-correlated 设定下优势更大（T=1: 0.109pp），但 worst 档假设 real errors closer to\n      i.i.d.，所以 block 优势在实际中不可达。\n      加权平均 iid advantage 仅 0.072pp——这是 worst 档下 per-test 方法的实际预期收益，\n      几乎没有实用意义。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 6: Oracle per-test advantage stratified by F2P test count\"\n        columns: [\"T (F2P count)\", \"% Instances\", \"iid Adv (pp)\", \"Block Adv (pp)\", \"Weighted iid Contrib\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 68.7, 0.020, 0.109, 0.014]\n          - [2, 15.8, 0.185, 0.362, 0.029]\n          - [\"3+\", 15.5, 0.312, 0.498, 0.048]\n          - [\"Weighted Avg\", 100.0, 0.072, 0.191, \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: x-axis T buckets, y-axis per-test advantage; area proportional to instance count shows dilution effect\"\n      - \"Pie chart showing T=1 dominance in SWE-bench Verified\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档叙事的核心支撑图表。视觉上清晰展示了\"理论优势存在但被分布稀释\"的故事。\n      T=1 的巨大占比（68.7%）使得 per-test 的理论优势在实践中几乎消失。\n      论文可以用这个 finding 作为 Claim 3 的\"negative characterization\"核心：\n      per-test 不是无用的，而是有用的条件（T≥2, block-correlated errors, regression rate >10%）\n      太少同时满足。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-repair Experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      给修复代理提供 per-test failure predictions vs 无 per-test 信息，\n      在 200 个 instances 上比较 resolve rate。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 28.5\n      with_diagnostic_resolve_rate: 29.0\n      resolve_rate_gain_pp: 0.5\n      gain_significant: false\n      p_value: 0.62\n      instances_where_diagnostic_helped: 4\n      instances_where_diagnostic_hurt: 3\n      net_helped: 1\n      diagnostic_precision_on_test_set: 78.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档 gain 在 [-0.5, 1] pp 范围。预测 +0.5pp（29.0% vs 28.5%），原因：\n      (1) 68.7% T=1 instances 中 per-test 信息与 trajectory-level 等价，提供 per-test\n      预测不增加任何信息；(2) 在 T≥2 instances（~31%，约 62/200 个）中，per-test 预测\n      的 precision ~78% 引入了约 22% 的错误诊断，修复代理可能基于错误信息做出更差的修复；\n      (3) 4 个 instances 中诊断确实帮助了定位（多测试场景中正确识别了失败的特定测试），\n      但 3 个 instances 中错误诊断反而误导了修复方向；(4) 净增益 1 个 instance（+0.5pp on 200），\n      统计上远不显著。\n      这确认了 worst 档假设：per-test diagnostics 的理论价值被预测噪声和 T=1 主导效应\n      共同消解。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 7: Diagnostic re-repair experiment\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve Rate (%), \"Δ vs Baseline\", p-value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"No diagnostic (baseline)\", 28.5, \"-\", \"-\"]\n          - [\"With per-test diagnostic\", 29.0, \"+0.5\", 0.62]\n          - [\"Oracle per-test (upper bound)\", 33.2, \"+4.7\", 0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: three conditions (baseline, predicted diagnostic, oracle diagnostic) showing oracle ceiling vs achievable gain\"\n    analysis: >\n      Oracle per-test 上界（33.2%）表明 per-test 信息在理想条件下有价值（+4.7pp），\n      但 predicted diagnostic 只能实现其中很小一部分（+0.5pp）。\n      Gap 来自两个方面：(a) 预测误差使诊断不可靠；(b) 修复代理本身对诊断信号的利用效率有限。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，Claim 2 被降级为\"hypothesis with oracle ceiling analysis\"，\n      不作为论文的实证贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练好的模型 per-test 预测中测量实际预测误差相关结构，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-correlated 仿真模型对比。\n    expected_results:\n      measured_intra_problem_error_correlation: 0.08\n      iid_expected_correlation: 0.0\n      block_model_assumed_correlation: 0.45\n      fraction_explained_by_iid: 0.82\n      fraction_explained_by_block: 0.18\n      cramer_v_problem_vs_error: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：\"block correlation effect weaker than simulated — real errors closer to i.i.d.\"\n      实测 intra-problem error correlation 仅 0.08（接近 i.i.d. 的 0.0，远低于 block model\n      假设的 0.45）。这意味着同一问题不同测试的预测误差之间几乎独立。\n      原因：(1) 模型对每个 (code, test) 对独立做前向传播，没有跨测试的信息共享，因此误差\n      不自然聚类；(2) function-level 测试之间差异较大（不同输入-输出对），即使对同一函数，\n      不同测试的难度分布接近均匀而非聚类；(3) Cramér's V = 0.06 表明 problem_id 对误差\n      模式几乎没有解释力。\n      这直接打击了 oracle simulation 中 block-correlated 设定的外部有效性——那些设定下\n      per-test 优势高达 0.36-0.50pp，但如果实际是近 i.i.d.，优势降至 0.02-0.07pp。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 8: Prediction error correlation structure\"\n        columns: [Model, \"Intra-problem ρ\", \"Per-test Adv (oracle, pp)\", \"Fit to Data (R²)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"i.i.d. (ρ=0)\", 0.00, \"0.020–0.072\", 0.82]\n          - [\"Block (ρ=0.45)\", 0.45, \"0.109–0.498\", 0.18]\n          - [\"Measured\", 0.08, \"0.025–0.095 (interpolated)\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot of predicted errors for test pairs within same problem, showing near-zero correlation\"\n      - \"QQ plot of empirical error correlation vs i.i.d. and block model predictions\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档中 Claim 3 \"negative characterization\" 的关键实证。\n      Oracle simulation 的 block-correlated 设定 over-estimated per-test advantage by ~5×。\n      论文应诚实报告这一点：block correlation 是理论上合理的假设，但在 4B LoRA 模型的\n      实际预测中不成立。这不否定 oracle 分析的价值——它揭示了 per-test 有用的理论条件——\n      但将 \"when does per-test help?\" 的答案从 \"often\" 修正为 \"rarely in practice\"。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Per-Test Dataset Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重新评估 SWE-bench Verified patches，提取 per-test labels。\n      构建 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据集（500 instances × 16 candidates）。\n    expected_results:\n      total_instances_attempted: 500\n      successful_evaluations: 462\n      failed_docker_builds: 23\n      timeout_evaluations: 15\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 117408\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 15.9\n      avg_f2p_tests_per_instance: 2.3\n      avg_p2p_tests_per_instance: 13.6\n      pass_rate_overall: 0.71\n      fail_rate_overall: 0.29\n      construction_time_hours: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      数据集构建本身是工程任务，worst 档不影响其成功率——Docker 评估的失败率（23 build failures\n      + 15 timeouts = 7.6%）来自 SWE-bench 已知的环境不稳定性而非方法论问题。\n      关键数据特征：avg F2P tests = 2.3（与 oracle simulation 的 T_mean=2.3 一致），\n      avg P2P tests = 13.6，说明 repo-level 确实有更多测试可以利用 per-test 粒度。\n      但 worst 档下这些额外测试不会转化为 per-test 优势（见 repo-level-training 预测）。\n      Pass rate 71% 表示大多数 candidate patches 通过大多数测试——修复任务的 baseline\n      不低，这使得增量改进更难显著。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 9: SWE-bench-PerTest dataset statistics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Instances (successful), 462]\n          - [Candidates per instance, \"16 (mean)\"]\n          - [Total (code, test) pairs, \"117,408\"]\n          - [F2P tests per instance (mean), 2.3]\n          - [P2P tests per instance (mean), 13.6]\n          - [Overall pass rate, \"71%\"]\n          - [Overall fail rate, \"29%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram of F2P test count distribution, confirming T=1 mode and long tail\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据集本身是一个 resource contribution，即使在 worst 档下也有独立价值。\n      分布特征确认了 oracle simulation 的假设（T distribution, pass/fail ratio），\n      为后续 repo-level experiments 提供了可靠的数据基础。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training (Classification vs CWM)\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上微调 Qwen3-4B/8B classification 和 CWM 模型，\n      评估 repo-level 性能和 cls vs cwm gap。\n    expected_results:\n      cls_4b_repo_f1: 73.8\n      cwm_4b_repo_f1: 73.2\n      cls_vs_cwm_4b_gap_pp: 0.6\n      cls_8b_repo_f1: 76.5\n      cwm_8b_repo_f1: 76.1\n      cls_vs_cwm_8b_gap_pp: 0.4\n      cwm_4b_unparseable_pct: 3.8\n      cwm_4b_truncated_pct: 1.2\n      cwm_8b_unparseable_pct: 2.1\n      cwm_8b_truncated_pct: 0.8\n      cwm_4b_exact_match: 52.3\n      cwm_8b_exact_match: 58.7\n      func_to_repo_cls_drop_pp: 13.7\n      func_to_repo_cwm_drop_pp: 14.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：\"CWM handles repo-level adequately (Qwen3-4B learns to compress/summarize traces)\"\n      和 \"Classification ≈ generation at repo-level\"。\n      \n      Repo-level gap 仅 0.6pp (4B) / 0.4pp (8B)，在 worst 档范围 [-1, 2] 内偏低端。原因：\n      (1) Qwen3-4B 学会了对 repo-level 长输出进行摘要式预测——不精确复现完整 trace，但\n      输出足够接近以判断 pass/fail。CWM 的 exact match 低（52.3%），但因为模型学到了\n      \"输出的关键语义模式\"（如 assertion error keywords、expected vs actual 值的判断），\n      即使字面不匹配，分类判断仍然正确；\n      (2) unparseable + truncated 仅 5%（3.8% + 1.2%），在 worst 档范围 [0, 5] 上限，\n      说明模型确实学会了在 token budget 内生成可解析的输出；\n      (3) 两种方法从 func-level 到 repo-level 都下降了 ~14pp（cls: 87.5→73.8, cwm: 87.5→73.2），\n      下降程度几乎相同，说明复杂度增加对两种方法的影响是均匀的；\n      (4) 8B 模型下 gap 更小（0.4pp），进一步确认等价性随规模增大而加强。\n      \n      这是 worst 档的定义性结果：repo-level 也没有打破等价性。论文必须完全放弃\n      \"complexity-dependent advantage\" 的 framing。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 10: Repo-level Classification vs CWM (SWE-bench-PerTest)\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, F1, \"Exact Match\", \"Unparseable %\", \"Truncated %\", \"Δ Cls−CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 4B, 73.8, \"-\", 0.0, 0.0, \"+0.6\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, 73.2, 52.3, 3.8, 1.2, \"-\"]\n          - [Classification, 8B, 76.5, \"-\", 0.0, 0.0, \"+0.4\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 8B, 76.1, 58.7, 2.1, 0.8, \"-\"]\n      - caption: \"Table 11: Function-level to Repo-level performance drop\"\n        columns: [Method, \"Func F1\", \"Repo F1\", \"Drop (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 87.5, 73.8, -13.7]\n          - [CWM Generation, 87.5, 73.2, -14.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: func-level vs repo-level F1 for cls and CWM, showing parallel drop\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: CWM exact match vs binary accuracy on repo-level, showing low exact match can coexist with decent binary accuracy\"\n    analysis: >\n      CWM 的 exact match 从 func-level 84% 暴跌至 repo-level 52%，但 F1 仅从 87.5 降至 73.2。\n      这个 disconnect 是 worst 档的核心反直觉发现：CWM 的\"失败模式\"（truncation、近似输出）\n      并没有导致分类性能的对应崩溃，因为模型学会了从不完美的生成中仍然提取 pass/fail 信号。\n      这挑战了原始论文 framing 中\"CWM failure modes dominate at repo-level\"的假设。\n      \n      论文 pivot：这个发现本身是有趣的分析贡献——\"为什么 generation 在字面意义上失败\n      但在语义意义上成功\"可以成为分析论文的一个 section。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge baseline（trajectory-level 和 per-test），\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的参考点。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_f1: 68.5\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_f1: 66.2\n      qwen3_32b_traj_f1: 74.8\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_f1: 73.1\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_unparseable_pct: 8.3\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_unparseable_pct: 4.1\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_8b_gap: 19.0\n      finetuned_4b_vs_zeroshot_32b_gap: 12.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM-as-judge 在 function-level 上表现显著低于微调 4B 模型，因为：\n      (1) 没有针对特定 pass/fail 判断格式的训练，输出不稳定且 unparseable 率较高；\n      (2) 32B 的上下文理解能力更强，缩小了差距但仍低于微调 4B（74.8 vs 87.5），\n      说明 task-specific fine-tuning 的价值大于 model scale 的差异；\n      (3) per-test 始终略低于 trajectory（~2pp），因为 zero-shot 模型需要更明确的\n      判断格式指导，per-test 的结构化输出对 zero-shot 更难。\n      在 worst 档叙事中，这些 baseline 提供 Pareto frontier 参考：\n      fine-tuned 4B > zero-shot 32B >> zero-shot 8B，确认 fine-tuning 是必要的。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 12: LLM-as-Judge baselines vs fine-tuned models\"\n        columns: [Method, Size, Fine-tuned, \"Traj F1\", \"Per-test F1\", \"Unparseable %\"]\n        rows:\n          - [LLM-Judge, 8B, No, 68.5, 66.2, 8.3]\n          - [LLM-Judge, 32B, No, 74.8, 73.1, 4.1]\n          - [Classification, 4B, Yes, \"-\", 87.5, 0.0]\n          - [CWM Generation, 4B, Yes, \"-\", 87.5, 0.0]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier plot: x-axis = model size (or FLOPs), y-axis = F1, showing fine-tuned 4B dominating zero-shot 32B\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B 显著优于 zero-shot 32B 这一结果在任何 tier 下都成立，\n      不受 worst 档的 cls-vs-cwm 等价性影响。这为 pivot 论文提供了一个次要但\n      坚实的贡献：即使 classification 和 generation 等价，fine-tuning 的效率优势\n      （4B fine-tuned > 32B zero-shot）是明确的实用结论。\n\n  - name: \"Per-test Majority Voting\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Per-test majority voting (K=3)，测试 self-consistency 是否提升 per-test 准确率。\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 87.5\n      majority_k3_pass_f1: 88.3\n      majority_k3_fail_f1: 88.9\n      majority_k3_overall_acc: 88.6\n      gain_from_voting_pp: 1.1\n      voting_vs_8b_single_pass: -1.5\n      inference_cost_multiplier: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 带来温和提升（+1.1pp），因为 self-consistency 修正了部分边界\n      预测。但收益有限的原因：(1) 4B 模型的 3 次推理采样在大多数 confident predictions\n      上完全一致（~85% 的测试三次结果相同），仅 ~15% 的 uncertain cases 从投票中受益；\n      (2) 3× inference cost 换取 1.1pp gain 的 cost-effectiveness 远低于直接用 8B\n      单次推理（+2.6pp）；(3) 在 worst 档下，voting 对 cls 和 cwm 的提升幅度相似，\n      不改变两者等价的结论。\n      这是 P2 优先级实验，在 worst 档叙事中仅作为 minor practical note。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Table 13: Majority voting ablation\"\n        columns: [Method, K, F1, \"Δ vs K=1\", \"Cost (×)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 1, 87.5, \"-\", \"1×\"]\n          - [Classification, 3, 88.6, \"+1.1\", \"3×\"]\n          - [Classification (8B), 1, 90.1, \"+2.6\", \"~2× (params)\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Voting 是一个合理但不显著的优化。在 worst 档 pivot 论文中，\n      可以在 appendix 中报告以展示方法的 thoroughness，但不影响核心叙事。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c5a97b80-9229-4bf1-bd6c-e99b19524a4a","total_cost_usd":0.391818,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10614,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":12556,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10614,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12556,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10614},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5570,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0056500000000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12556,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10614,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.386168,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_